<title>USA: K&amp;G Men's Center sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>K&amp;G Men's Center sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>K&amp;G Men's Center Inc said on Friday it declared a three-for-two stock split in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend, payable on April 25 to shareholders of record as of April 7.</p>
<p>K&amp;G is a superstore retailer of a complete line of men's apparel and accessories, operating 18 stores in 11 states.</p>
<p>K&amp;G shares were trading at 26-3/4 early Friday, up 1-1/4 on the day.  Their 52-week high was 30-1/8.</p>
